Ddoc

$(COMMUNITY D Language Foundation AI Contribution Policy,

$(HEADERNAV_TOC)

$(P DLF does not prohibit code contributions generated in part or in full by an LLM. Such code must satisfy the same
quality, security, maintainability, and review standards expected of any code submitted to DLF repositories. The following
principles are applied to all contributions, irrespective of the tools used to prepare them:
)

$(OL
        $(LI $(B Contributor responsibility.) A contributor must have the authority to submit the contribution under the
        applicable project license and must take responsibility for the submitted code.)
        $(LI $(B Human understanding and review.) Code must not be merged merely because an AI system produced
        something that appears to work. The contributor and reviewers must be able to understand, evaluate, test,
        and maintain it.)
        $(LI $(B No relaxation of engineering standards.) AI-assisted contributions are subject to the same architectural,
        correctness, portability, performance, documentation, testing, and review requirements as other contributions.)
        $(LI $(B Provenance concerns.) Where a contribution contains suspiciously distinctive material, unexplained changes in
        style, or other indications of possible copying, maintainers may request further information, require rewriting,
        or reject the contribution.)
        $(LI $(B Response to credible claims.) DLF will investigate credible allegations that code incorporated into its projects
        infringes third-party rights and will take appropriate corrective action where warranted.)
))


Macros:
        TITLE=D Language Foundation AI Contribution Policy
        SUBNAV=$(SUBNAV_ARTICLES)
